        "original_id": "8e8f6c2d-489d-5161-b1d3-9244b378941b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Longkou, Changle District, Shandong province, China, Bohai Sea, Laizhou Bay, East China Sea, Mawei District, Min River\n- People: Lu Min\n- Roles: flying ace\n- Events: Korean War\n\nFacts:\n- Longkou, formerly called Huang County, is a port city in northeastern Shandong province, China.\n- Longkou faces the Bohai Sea to the north and Laizhou Bay to the west.\n- Changle District faces the East China Sea and is connected to Mawei District by the Min River.\n- Lu Min was born in Longkou, Shandong Province.\n- Lu Min was a flying ace during the Korean War and achieved eight victories.",
